@* Infinity Atom Certification Exam Candidate Agreement (pre-exam screen 1). *@

<div class="pre-card agreement">
    <div class="pre-art">
        <h1 class="pre-art-ttl">
            <span>Infinity Atom</span>
            <span>Certification Exam</span>
            <span>Candidate Agreement</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="pre-art-sub">August, 2026</p>
        <div class="pre-art-stack" aria-hidden="true">
            <span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pre-body">
        <p><strong>
            When you registered for this exam, you agreed to adhere to the terms and
            conditions of the Infinity Atom Certification Exam Candidate Agreement. The
            following information provides a reminder of the rules specific to the
            exam experience.
        </strong></p>

        <p>This exam is Infinity Atom confidential and proprietary information and is
           protected by intellectual property laws.</p>

        <p>You will not participate in any behavior that could compromise the
           confidentiality or results of any Infinity Atom Certification exam. Proctors
           are authorized to take immediate and appropriate measures against
           individuals who violate testing rules. Examples of misconduct include but
           are not limited to:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>Capturing or providing access in any form or by any means to any exam,
                exam content, or exam-related information.</li>
            <li>Misrepresenting your identity or impersonating another individual.</li>
            <li>Misrepresenting your country of residence or the country in which an
                online proctored exam will be delivered.</li>
            <li>Modifying or altering the exam, exam score, or any exam record.</li>
            <li>Submitting any work or answers that are not entirely your own.</li>
            <li>Using Artificial Intelligence or related products or services in any
                way to assist you.</li>
            <li>Providing or receiving improper assistance during the exam.</li>
            <li>Seeking or obtaining unauthorized access to any exam, exam content, or
                exam-related information.</li>
            <li>Possessing non-authorized items while taking an exam, including mobile
                phones, electronic devices, laptops, watches, notes, documentation, or
                content.</li>
            <li>Misconduct as determined by statistical analysis or any other
                misconduct that could compromise the confidentiality, integrity, or
                security of the exam.</li>
            <li>Violating any Infinity Atom or exam delivery provider's policy,
                requirement, or rule.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Infinity Atom reserves the right to invalidate your exam score and/or ban you
           from the Credentialing Program if Infinity Atom determines you were not
           compliant with these rules.</p>

        <div class="pre-actions">
            <button type="button" class="pre-link" @onclick="OnDecline">No, I don't agree</button>
            <button type="button" class="pre-btn" @onclick="OnAccept">Yes, I agree</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnAccept { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnDecline { get; set; }
}
